<title>GREECE: CITIBANK JACKS UP SOME BASE LOAN RATES.</title>
<headline>CITIBANK JACKS UP SOME BASE LOAN RATES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citibank will raise its base</p>
<p>lending rates for working capital by 100 basis points and freely</p>
<p>investible funds and business and professional by 50 basis</p>
<p>points effective Tuesday, it said in a statement. All other</p>
<p>lending rates were unchanged.</p>
<p>Citibank, which reviews its rates weekly, offers the</p>
<p>following rate structure:</p>
<p>** Base rate for working capital loans at 18.25 percent from</p>
<p>17.25 percent</p>
<p>** Business and professional base lending rate from 19 percent</p>
<p>from 18.50 percent</p>
<p>** Special base rate for public enterprises and organisations</p>
<p>(DEKO) at 18.25 percent</p>
<p>** Base rate for freely investible funds at 18.50 percent from</p>
<p>18.00 percent</p>
<p>** Mortgage rate at 17.25 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans at 24 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans with invoices at 23 percent</p>
<p>** Auto loans at 19.75 percent</p>
<p>Contribution under Law 128 is not included in the rates</p>
<p>quoted, it said.</p>
<p>Rates on working capital loans denominated in foreign</p>
<p>currency for the coming week will be:</p>
<p>    US Dollars     :  7.98 percent</p>
<p>    Marks	    :  5.66 percent</p>
<p>    Yen		:  2.93 percent</p>
<p>    Guilders	 :  5.56 percent</p>
<p>    Ecu		:  6.70 percent</p>
<p>Pounds Sterling:  8.87 percent</p>
<p>French francs  :  6.00 percent</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
